## Quick Reference: Lesson 003

### ROM Character Set

| Property | Value | Notes |
|----------|-------|-------|
| Start address | $3D00 | First character (space) |
| End address | $3FFF | Last character (©) |
| Total size | 768 bytes | 96 characters × 8 bytes |
| Bytes per char | 8 | One byte per scanline |
| First ASCII | 32 | Space character |
| Last ASCII | 127 | Copyright symbol |

### Address Calculation

**ROM character address:**
```
ROM_ADDR = $3D00 + ((ASCII - 32) × 8)

Examples:
  "A" (65): $3D00 + ((65-32) × 8) = $3E08
  "0" (48): $3D00 + ((48-32) × 8) = $3D80
  "a" (97): $3D00 + ((97-32) × 8) = $3F08
```

**Screen address (top third only):**
```
SCREEN_ADDR = $4000 + (row × 256) + column

Examples:
  Row 0, col 0: $4000
  Row 1, col 15: $4100 + 15 = $410F
  Row 7, col 31: $4700 + 31 = $471F
```

### Scanline Spacing

| Area | Spacing | Technique |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Top third (rows 0-7) | +256 bytes | `INC D` |
| Middle third (rows 8-15) | Complex | Thirds formula |
| Bottom third (rows 16-23) | Complex | Thirds formula |

### Instructions Used

| Instruction | Purpose | T-states | Bytes |
|-------------|---------|----------|-------|
| LD HL,nn | Load ROM address | 10 | 3 |
| LD DE,nn | Load screen address | 10 | 3 |
| LD B,n | Load loop counter | 7 | 2 |
| LD A,(HL) | Read from ROM | 7 | 1 |
| LD (DE),A | Write to screen | 7 | 1 |
| INC HL | Next ROM byte | 6 | 1 |
| INC D | Next scanline (+256) | 4 | 1 |
| DJNZ label | Loop if B ≠ 0 | 13/8 | 2 |
| CALL label | Call subroutine | 17 | 3 |
| RET | Return from subroutine | 10 | 1 |

### Performance Comparison

| Operation | Assembly | BASIC | Advantage |
|-----------|----------|-------|-----------|
| Display 1 char | ~320 T-states | ~5000 T-states | ~15× faster |
| Display "HI" | ~660 T-states | ~10000 T-states | ~15× faster |
| Display line of text | ~5000 T-states | ~80000 T-states | ~16× faster |

