## What You've Learnt

After completing this lesson, you can:

- ✓ Locate ROM character set at $3D00-$3FFF
- ✓ Calculate ROM address for any ASCII character
- ✓ Understand character bitmap format (8 bytes per character)
- ✓ Copy character bitmaps from ROM to screen
- ✓ Use `INC D` to navigate scanlines (+256 bytes)
- ✓ Create subroutines with CALL/RET
- ✓ Display multiple characters with code reuse
- ✓ Understand why Spectrum text display differs from character-based computers
- ✓ Calculate screen addresses in top third of screen

**Key insight:** Characters are pre-designed pixel patterns in ROM. Displaying text = copying pixel data, not writing character codes. This gives you complete control over every pixel.

**Next lesson:** Reading Back - We'll learn to read from screen memory and use the CP instruction to check if a position is occupied. Essential for collision detection in games!

